                <pb facs="0196" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.152H11/434: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-13T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 13,
                                1920—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>66. George B. Hayes, attorney for McGivney Rokeby Construction Company is leaving
                    for Havana to represent Company in proposed settlement of claim against Cuban
                    Government. He will arrive Havana Friday morning next, at latest.</p>
                <p>Afford all possible and proper assistance in bringing about settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
